# Source drops and working files. Raw renders, supplier photography and archives
# get normalised into assets/<product>/*.webp before use; the originals stay out of
# the repo. Several are 2 MB+ each, and assets/greenlightpics is ~25 MB of imagery
# the README documents as AI-generated and unusable.
#
# Only .webp is tracked under assets/<product>/, so a new product folder is covered
# automatically rather than needing another line here.
*.zip
assets/greenlightpics/
assets/*/*.png
assets/*/*.jpg
assets/*/*.jpeg
# Real assets live flat at assets/<product>/<name>.webp, so anything nested one
# level deeper is a source-drop folder (e.g. "assets/panel/Panel New/").
assets/*/*/
# Source .webp drops (only .png/.jpg are covered by the patterns above).
assets/mask/women lounging.webp
assets/mask/TLM300PRO-L-LED-Face-Mask2-768x768.webp

# Generated by tools/build-site.js. Vercel regenerates it on every deploy;
# committing it would let a stale build outlive its source.
build/

# Vercel CLI local link state.
.vercel/

# Claude Design paste dumps and duplicate exports that shipped inside the
# approved set. Referenced by no page, hashed in no approval record, and never
# read by tools/build-site.js. The 18 .webp files here are byte-identical to
# Calmlyte Approved Site/assets/, which is tracked. Kept on disk as part of the
# delivered artifact; not carried in the tracked set.
Calmlyte Approved Site/uploads/

# Shopify Storefront token. Read from the environment by
# tools/resolve-variants.js and never written to a tracked file; these patterns
# exist so a local .env cannot be committed by accident. The Storefront token is
# publishable, but an Admin token is not and must never land here.
.env
.env.*

# Deployed favicon and social-preview assets. Not a source drop: these are the
# exact bytes the build copies to the output root and /assets, so they have to be
# in the tracked set or a clean checkout — which is what Vercel builds — has
# nothing to copy and the build fails. Re-included as a directory because the
# assets/*/*/ rule above excludes it, and git will not descend into an excluded
# directory to pick individual files back out. ~150 KB total.
!assets/8.30.26/favicon/
